% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-27 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: non_resolving pulmonary consolidation workup
%   (the diagnostic approach to a lobar/segmental consolidative opacity that
%   persists essentially unchanged over months despite full antibacterial AND
%   anti-tuberculous therapy in a lifelong non-smoker), NOT a single diagnosis.
%
% The central diagnostic puzzle the IR poses (q1-q4): a 52-year-old lifelong
% non-smoking woman with a right-lower-lobe DENSE CONSOLIDATION + an exudative,
% LYMPHOCYTE-RICH, LOW-GLUCOSE pleural effusion, NEGATIVE cultures (fluid,
% blood, sputum, bronchial washings), a pleural ADA of 18.6 U/L (BELOW the
% conventional 40 U/L TB cutoff), NO cavitation, and a band of consolidative
% opacity that does NOT change on serial CT at 2 and 6 months and does NOT
% respond to EITHER antibiotics OR a 6-month empirical anti-TB regimen. A
% transbronchial biopsy then yields ATYPICAL LYMPHOID CELLS, prompting a
% CT-guided core biopsy plus staging-style upper-GI endoscopy with gastric
% biopsies and a bone-marrow trephine.
%
% That conjunction -- an indolent non-resolving consolidation in a non-smoker,
% a lymphocyte-rich exudate, atypical lymphoid cells on lung tissue, and a
% staging workup reaching for OTHER mucosal sites (stomach) and marrow -- is the
% textbook picture of PRIMARY PULMONARY MALT LYMPHOMA (extranodal marginal-zone
% lymphoma of bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue, "BALToma"), the classic
% great mimic of non-resolving pneumonia.
%
% Magnitudes are encoded QUALITATIVELY per adj-lang grammar (no leading digit,
% no uppercase identifiers). E.g. pleural_ada(below_tb_cutoff),
% consolidation_course(unchanged_over_months).
%
% Anti-overfit note: every clause is added because a cited source supports the
% DIRECTION of the likelihood ratio for that finding in that disease, NOT to make
% this case land on a chosen answer. Discriminators that argue AGAINST the
% tempting wrong answers (presumed TB; pneumonic-type adenocarcinoma, which is
% ALSO classic in non-smoking women) carry LR<1 where a source supports them.
% Correlated findings that are ONE mechanism (the indolent-lymphoid gestalt; the
% non-resolution-despite-therapy gestalt) are grouped under a single mechanism
% directive so the combined likelihood ratio fires ONCE and does not double-count.
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates among non-resolving-consolidation workups) =====

% rationale: among non-resolving consolidations driven to tissue biopsy, an
% indolent primary pulmonary lymphoma (overwhelmingly low-grade MALT type) is a
% recognized, classically under-considered cause; given the lymphoid biopsy and
% multi-site staging it carries a substantial pretest probability here.
prior 0.26 for diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2016;47:1244 (Pulmonary MALT lymphoma revisited: indolent, mimics non-resolving pneumonia)" trust authoritative

% rationale: pneumonic-type / mucinous lung adenocarcinoma is THE other neoplastic
% great-mimic of non-resolving consolidation and, like this patient, classically
% occurs in non-smokers and women -- so it must be argued down on tissue, not prior.
prior 0.22 for diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2023;13:1234291 (consolidation pattern of MALT vs pneumonic-type lung adenocarcinoma)" trust authoritative

% rationale: TB was the presumed (and treated) diagnosis; in a lymphocyte-rich
% exudate TB is the canonical concern, which is exactly why empirical anti-TB was
% started -- high enough prior that the engine must EARN the move away from it.
prior 0.20 for diagnosis(tuberculous_pleuropulmonary_disease)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2003;21:220 (ADA in lymphocytic effusions; TB the default lymphocytic-exudate concern)" trust authoritative

% rationale: organizing pneumonia is a standard non-infectious cause of a
% consolidation unresponsive to antibiotics and belongs on the differential.
prior 0.10 for diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "Merck Manual Prof, Cryptogenic Organizing Pneumonia (consolidation unresponsive to antibiotics)" trust authoritative

% rationale: ordinary severe community-acquired pneumonia with a parapneumonic
% effusion was the initial working diagnosis; kept low because the defining feature
% of this case is FAILURE to resolve, which an ordinary bacterial pneumonia does not do.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(community_acquired_pneumonia)
  source "Radiology Assistant, Chest X-Ray Lung Disease (CAP consolidation resolves with treatment)" trust authoritative

% ===== SHARED INDOLENT-LYMPHOID SIGNATURE (ONE mechanism, lymphoma) =====
% rationale: the constellation -- atypical lymphoid cells on lung tissue, a
% LYMPHOCYTE-RICH exudate, an indolent course with the patient remaining
% relatively well, and a staging reach toward OTHER mucosal sites (stomach) and
% marrow -- is ONE correlated syndrome (the clinicopathologic phenotype of an
% indolent B-cell / MALT lymphoma), NOT several independent facts. Counting each
% separately would double-count correlated evidence and saturate the posterior, so
% it fires ONCE as a single combined likelihood ratio.
% mechanism indolent_lymphoid_phenotype for diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma) lr 9.0 : histology(atypical_lymphoid_cells_on_lung_tissue), pleural_fluid(lymphocyte_rich), clinical_course(indolent_relatively_well), staging_workup(other_mucosal_and_marrow_sites)

% ===== SHARED NON-RESOLUTION-DESPITE-THERAPY SIGNATURE (ONE mechanism) =====
% rationale: the SAME stubborn opacity -- unchanged on serial CT over months and
% failing BOTH antibacterial AND anti-TB therapy -- is ONE correlated "this is not
% an ordinary treatable infection" gestalt. It raises any indolent neoplastic
% explanation (here the MALT lymphoma) once, rather than once per failed therapy.
% mechanism non_resolution_despite_therapy for diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma) lr 3.5 : consolidation_course(unchanged_over_months), treatment_response(no_response_to_antibiotics), treatment_response(no_response_to_anti_tb)

% ===== PRIMARY PULMONARY MALT LYMPHOMA (the unifying answer) =====

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR -- atypical lymphoid cells on lung tissue is the
% pivotal finding that reframes the whole case from infection toward a lymphoid
% neoplasm; in the right context it points specifically at primary pulmonary
% lymphoma (MALT type). Kept as an independent edge ON TOP of the shared mechanism
% because sources single it out as the decisive morphologic clue.
contributes 5.0 from histology(atypical_lymphoid_cells_on_lung_tissue) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "PMC12209244 (pulmonary MALT lymphoma: atypical lymphoid infiltrate; tissue with lymphoepithelial lesions/light-chain restriction)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a staging-style reach to upper-GI endoscopy with gastric biopsies and
% a bone-marrow trephine is precisely the workup for a suspected MALT lymphoma --
% concomitant disease at other mucosal sites occurs in ~25-35% and marrow
% involvement in ~13-30%, so this multi-site staging is near-specific for it.
contributes 4.0 from staging_workup(other_mucosal_and_marrow_sites) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2016;47:1244 (MALT lymphoma: other-site mucosal involvement 25-35%, marrow 13-30%; stage with GI/marrow)" trust authoritative

% rationale: an indolent course -- the patient remains relatively well with only
% low-grade intermittent symptoms despite a persisting opacity -- is characteristic
% of low-grade pulmonary MALT lymphoma and atypical for an aggressive infection or
% high-grade tumor.
contributes 2.5 from clinical_course(indolent_relatively_well) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2009;34:1408 (pulmonary MALT lymphoma: indolent, often mildly symptomatic)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a lymphocyte-rich exudate accompanying the consolidation is consistent
% with lymphomatous pleural involvement and supports a lymphoid process over a
% pyogenic one.
contributes 1.8 from pleural_fluid(lymphocyte_rich) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2003;21:220 (lymphoma among non-TB causes of a lymphocyte-rich exudate)" trust authoritative

% rationale: an exudate by Light's criteria with a high pleural LDH is consistent
% with malignant/lymphomatous pleural involvement (a non-specific but supportive edge).
contributes 1.3 from pleural_fluid(exudate_high_ldh) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "ScienceDirect, Pulmonary Consolidation overview (exudative effusion in pulmonary lymphoma)" trust authoritative

% rationale: persistent culture-negativity across fluid, blood, sputum AND
% bronchial washings argues against an ongoing pyogenic/mycobacterial infection and
% is the expected microbiology of a neoplastic consolidation.
contributes 1.6 from microbiology(persistently_culture_negative) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "MDPI 2025;85:202 (pulmonary MALT lymphoma as non-resolving pneumonia: repeatedly negative microbiology)" trust authoritative

% ===== PNEUMONIC-TYPE ADENOCARCINOMA (the OTHER non-smoker great-mimic) =====

% rationale: pneumonic-type mucinous adenocarcinoma classically presents as a
% non-resolving consolidation in non-smokers/women and fails to respond to
% antibiotics -- a real positive edge for the non-resolution picture.
contributes 1.8 from treatment_response(no_response_to_antibiotics) to diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "PMC8203063 (pneumonic-type adenocarcinoma: non-resolving consolidation, poor antibiotic response)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a persisting unchanged opacity is compatible with an indolent
% pneumonic-type adenocarcinoma.
contributes 1.5 from consolidation_course(unchanged_over_months) to diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "Springer Insights Imaging 2021;12 (pneumonic-type lung adenocarcinoma: persistent consolidation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- the diagnostic lung tissue contained
% ATYPICAL LYMPHOID cells, not malignant glandular/epithelial cells; lymphoid
% morphology argues specifically AWAY from an adenocarcinoma.
contributes 0.2 from histology(atypical_lymphoid_cells_on_lung_tissue) to diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2023;13:1234291 (adenocarcinoma is glandular/epithelial; lymphoid infiltrate distinguishes MALT lymphoma)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- a staging reach to OTHER mucosal
% sites (gastric) and marrow is a lymphoma-staging strategy, not the workup of a
% lung adenocarcinoma, and points away from a primary epithelial lung cancer.
contributes 0.5 from staging_workup(other_mucosal_and_marrow_sites) to diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2016;47:1244 (multi-mucosal-site + marrow staging is the MALT-lymphoma pathway)" trust inferred

% ===== TUBERCULOUS PLEUROPULMONARY DISEASE (the presumed-and-treated answer) =====

% rationale: a lymphocyte-rich exudate is the classic profile of tuberculous
% pleurisy, the reason TB was presumed and empirically treated. Real positive edge,
% but non-specific -- lymphoma and other causes share it.
contributes 1.6 from pleural_fluid(lymphocyte_rich) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pleuropulmonary_disease)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2003;21:220 (TB the leading cause of lymphocyte-predominant exudates)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- the pleural ADA of 18.6 U/L is BELOW
% the conventional 40 U/L cutoff for tuberculous pleurisy; a sub-threshold ADA in a
% lymphocytic effusion has a ~99% negative predictive value for TB, so it argues
% strongly AGAINST the presumed TB despite the "modestly raised" framing.
contributes 0.15 from pleural_ada(below_tb_cutoff) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pleuropulmonary_disease)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2003;21:220 (ADA <40 U/L in lymphocytic effusion: NPV ~99% for TB)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- ABSENCE of cavitation over months on
% serial imaging is atypical for the kind of progressive pulmonary TB that would
% explain a fixed parenchymal opacity, weakly arguing against active TB.
contributes 0.6 from imaging(no_cavitation) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pleuropulmonary_disease)
  source "Radiology Assistant, Chest X-Ray Lung Disease (cavitation typical of post-primary pulmonary TB)" trust inferred

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- failure of a FULL 6-month empirical
% anti-TB regimen to change the opacity at all is strong evidence the process is not
% treatment-responsive tuberculosis.
contributes 0.25 from treatment_response(no_response_to_anti_tb) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pleuropulmonary_disease)
  source "MDPI 2025;85:202 (non-response to anti-TB therapy argues against occult TB; reconsider lymphoma)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- atypical lymphoid cells on lung
% tissue are not the granulomatous picture of TB and point at a lymphoid neoplasm.
contributes 0.4 from histology(atypical_lymphoid_cells_on_lung_tissue) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pleuropulmonary_disease)
  source "PMC12209244 (atypical lymphoid infiltrate is not caseating granuloma; favors lymphoma over TB)" trust inferred

% ===== ORGANIZING PNEUMONIA =====

% rationale: organizing pneumonia characteristically does NOT respond to
% antibiotics, so a consolidation unresponsive to antibacterials fits it.
contributes 1.7 from treatment_response(no_response_to_antibiotics) to diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "Merck Manual Prof, Cryptogenic Organizing Pneumonia (does not respond to antibiotics)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- an opacity FIXED and unchanged over
% months is against organizing pneumonia, whose hallmark is migratory/waxing-waning
% opacities (and which characteristically responds to corticosteroids).
contributes 0.4 from consolidation_course(unchanged_over_months) to diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "Merck Manual Prof, COP (migratory opacities; corticosteroid-responsive, not fixed for months)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- atypical lymphoid cells are not the
% organizing fibroblastic plugs of organizing pneumonia and point away from it.
contributes 0.5 from histology(atypical_lymphoid_cells_on_lung_tissue) to diagnosis(organizing_pneumonia)
  source "Merck Manual Prof, COP (intraluminal organizing connective tissue, not atypical lymphoid cells)" trust inferred

% ===== ORDINARY COMMUNITY-ACQUIRED PNEUMONIA (the initial working diagnosis) =====

% rationale: the acute febrile presentation with neutrophilic leucocytosis, markedly
% raised CRP and lobar consolidation is the textbook entry picture of CAP -- which is
% exactly why it was the initial working diagnosis.
contributes 1.5 from presentation(acute_febrile_neutrophilic_lobar) to diagnosis(community_acquired_pneumonia)
  source "Radiology Assistant, Chest X-Ray Lung Disease (lobar consolidation + acute febrile illness = typical CAP)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- a consolidation that fails to clear
% after a FULL antibiotic course is the defining argument against ordinary bacterial
% CAP, which resolves with appropriate therapy.
contributes 0.2 from treatment_response(no_response_to_antibiotics) to diagnosis(community_acquired_pneumonia)
  source "MDPI 2025;85:202 (CAP resolves with antibiotics; non-resolution mandates a search for a mimic)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) -- persistent negativity of all cultures
% argues against a treatable pyogenic pneumonia.
contributes 0.5 from microbiology(persistently_culture_negative) to diagnosis(community_acquired_pneumonia)
  source "ScienceDirect, Pulmonary Consolidation overview (negative microbiology argues against pyogenic CAP)" trust inferred

% ===== NEXT STEP (definitive lymphoid tissue diagnosis) =====

% rationale: the decisive next step is to obtain ADEQUATE lung tissue with
% lymphoma-specific studies -- immunohistochemistry/flow for B-cell markers, light-
% chain restriction and immunoglobulin clonality -- on the core biopsy (or a
% cryobiopsy if needed), since a small transbronchial sample showing only "atypical
% lymphoid cells" cannot establish or exclude clonal MALT lymphoma.
prior 0.30 for next_step(core_or_cryo_biopsy_with_lymphoma_immunophenotyping)
  source "PMC12209244 (definitive MALT diagnosis needs larger tissue + immunophenotype/clonality; cryobiopsy after failed TBLB)" trust authoritative
contributes 5.0 from histology(atypical_lymphoid_cells_on_lung_tissue) to next_step(core_or_cryo_biopsy_with_lymphoma_immunophenotyping)
  source "PMC12209244 (atypical lymphoid cells -> obtain more tissue for immunophenotyping/clonality)" trust authoritative
contributes 3.0 from microbiology(persistently_culture_negative) to next_step(core_or_cryo_biopsy_with_lymphoma_immunophenotyping)
  source "MDPI 2025;85:202 (culture-negative non-resolving consolidation -> biopsy for tissue diagnosis)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.5 from consolidation_course(unchanged_over_months) to next_step(core_or_cryo_biopsy_with_lymphoma_immunophenotyping)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2016;47:1244 (persistent unexplained opacity -> definitive histology)" trust authoritative

% rationale: the alternative arm if a clonal lymphoid process is confirmed -- full
% lymphoma staging (the gastric biopsies + marrow trephine already arranged, plus
% PET/CT) -- to define extent. Lower prior because tissue confirmation comes first.
prior 0.12 for next_step(complete_lymphoma_staging)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2016;47:1244 (stage confirmed MALT lymphoma with GI, marrow, PET/CT)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.0 from staging_workup(other_mucosal_and_marrow_sites) to next_step(complete_lymphoma_staging)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2016;47:1244 (multi-site involvement -> complete staging)" trust authoritative

% ===== UNCERTAINTIES (decision-relevant, unresolved -- pending pathology) =====

% u-clonality: immunophenotyping / clonality on adequate tissue has not yet been
% reported. A MONOCLONAL B-cell result (light-chain restriction / Ig clonality) is
% near-dispositive for MALT lymphoma; a REACTIVE/polyclonal result argues strongly
% against and back toward a benign lymphoid hyperplasia or other cause. Highest VOI.
contributes 12.0 from immunophenotype(monoclonal_b_cell) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "PMC12209244 (light-chain restriction / monoclonal Ig rearrangement confirms MALT lymphoma)" trust authoritative
contributes 0.15 from immunophenotype(reactive_polyclonal) to diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "ERS Eur Respir J 2016;47:1244 (polyclonal/reactive lymphoid infiltrate argues against MALT lymphoma)" trust authoritative
uncertain { immunophenotype(monoclonal_b_cell), immunophenotype(reactive_polyclonal) } for diagnosis(pulmonary_malt_lymphoma)
  source "PMC12209244 (clonality/immunophenotype on adequate tissue not yet reported; decisive discriminator)"

% u-clonality vs adenocarcinoma: the same tissue result swings adenocarcinoma the
% other way -- a monoclonal B-cell result essentially excludes an epithelial tumor;
% a non-lymphoid/reactive result reopens the epithelial differential.
contributes 0.1 from immunophenotype(monoclonal_b_cell) to diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2023;13:1234291 (a clonal B-cell infiltrate is not an adenocarcinoma)" trust authoritative
contributes 1.5 from immunophenotype(reactive_polyclonal) to diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "Frontiers Oncol 2023;13:1234291 (no clonal lymphoid population -> reconsider an epithelial malignancy)" trust inferred
uncertain { immunophenotype(monoclonal_b_cell), immunophenotype(reactive_polyclonal) } for diagnosis(pneumonic_type_adenocarcinoma)
  source "PMC12209244 (tissue immunophenotype pending; result reclassifies lymphoid vs epithelial)"
